              <div>
                <strong>Maps</strong>
                <p>Use blank maps for geography and location-based facts.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <strong>Timelines</strong>
                <p>Put movements and historical events in chronological order.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <strong>Tables</strong>
                <p>Compare tribes, districts, schemes, industries and institutions.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <strong>Cause → Effect</strong>
                <p>Connect resources, industries, development and environmental issues.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <strong>Flash revision</strong>
                <p>Keep volatile facts in short lists for rapid recall.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <strong>MCQs</strong>
                <p>Turn passive reading into active retrieval through questions.</p>
              </div>
